# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added**: `@vercel/speed-insights@^2.0.0` to dependencies
- **Package Manager**: npm (with --legacy-peer-deps flag to resolve peer dependency conflicts)
- **Updated**: package.json and package-lock.json

### 2. Component Integration
- **Modified**: `src/app/layout.tsx`
- **Added Import**: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
- **Added Component**: `<SpeedInsights />` component placed at the end of the body tag in RootLayout

This follows the official Next.js App Router pattern for version 13.5+ as specified in the Vercel documentation.

## Implementation Details

The SpeedInsights component was added to the root layout file (`src/app/layout.tsx`) which is the correct location for Next.js App Router projects. The component is placed inside the `<body>` tag after the `{children}` element, ensuring it's loaded on every page of the application.

## Verification

All verification steps completed successfully:
- ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
- ✅ Linter passed with no issues  
- ✅ All tests passed (8/8 tests)
- ✅ TypeScript compilation successful

## Next Steps

To enable Speed Insights in your Vercel dashboard:
1. Navigate to your Vercel project dashboard
2. Select "Speed Insights" from the sidebar
3. Choose this project and click "Enable"
4. Deploy your changes to Vercel
5. Once deployed, Speed Insights will begin collecting performance metrics

The implementation is complete and ready for deployment.
